      "seed": 532246628,
      "version": 3842,
      "versionNonce": 835475526,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1773929483912,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-> In LangChain, \"models\" are the core interface through which you can\ninteract with Ai Models .\n\n-> as we know the LLMs are huge in size like 100gb of data, therefore\nit is not possible for normal/average individuals to use them by storing\nlocally on their server or sy stem.\n\n-> to solve this problem, big giants like google, openAi introduced their\napi keys, so one can directly make an api call and use the LLMs.    \n\n-> there's one more problem, different  api providers have different way\nof implementations, for eg - if a developer want to use two apis in \nsingle app, you have to write two different codes for them. \n\n-> Standardisation was needed, LangChain noticed this and thought\nto build an standard interface which can easily change the api provider,\nbut not the implementation for same, in simple words: LangChain,\nstandardised the implementation of different api provider out there.\n\n-> here the example of snippet\n>>> python\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-> In LangChain, \"models\" are the core interface through which you can\ninteract with Ai Models .\n\n-> as we know the LLMs are huge in size like 100gb of data, therefore\nit is not possible for normal/average individuals to use them by storing\nlocally on their server or sy stem.\n\n-> to solve this problem, big giants like google, openAi introduced their\napi keys, so one can directly make an api call and use the LLMs.    \n\n-> there's one more problem, different  api providers have different way\nof implementations, for eg - if a developer want to use two apis in \nsingle app, you have to write two different codes for them. \n\n-> Standardisation was needed, LangChain noticed this and thought\nto build an standard interface which can easily change the api provider,\nbut not the implementation for same, in simple words: LangChain,\nstandardised the implementation of different api provider out there.\n\n-> here the example of snippet\n>>> python\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
